course: dictionary
lesson: 8417
title: Runway: a strip for planes and models
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A runway is a long, flat strip of hard ground at an airport where planes take off and land. Read the words around it for clues. Planes, pilots and lights all point to flying, so that is the meaning here.
explain: A runway can also be the long, narrow stage that models walk along at a fashion show, also called a catwalk. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Runway numbers are a clue to direction. The number is the compass direction divided by ten. Runway 27 points to about 270 degrees, which is west, and the same strip seen from the other end is runway 09, pointing east.
fact: A runway is a long, flat strip of hard ground at an airport where planes take off and land.
fact: «Runways have lights to guide pilots in the dark and fog.»
fact: A plane needs a long runway to build up enough speed to take off.
fact: «Runway» can also mean the long, narrow stage that models walk along at a fashion show, also called a catwalk.
fact: On a compass, north is 0 or 360 degrees, east is 90, south is 180 and west is 270.
exercise: «Runways have lights to guide pilots in the dark and fog.» Who do the lights guide? | Children on a school trip | Bees in a garden | Shoppers in a mall | *Pilots
exercise: Mia says a runway is a flat field for football. What is a runway really? | A shelf in a shop | *A long, flat strip of hard ground where planes take off and land | A type of bread | A small pond in a park
exercise: At a fashion show, «The models walked slowly down the runway.» What does runway mean here? | A busy road | A flat airport strip | A long wooden bridge | *A long, narrow stage
test: «Runway 27 points west.» Why does runway 27 point west? | *Because 27 divided by ten is about 270 degrees, which is west on a compass | Because it is painted in a westerly colour | Because pilots like the number 27 | Because 27 is the number of planes
test: Which compass direction does runway 09 point to? | South | *East | West | North
exam: Ruby says, «The same strip is runway 27 from one end and runway 09 from the other.» Why are the two numbers different? | Ruby has made a mistake, because they must be the same | The numbers were picked at random | *The two ends point in opposite directions, west and east | One number is for planes and one is for models
